# Main session manual: file functions, connectivity, run recipes. Claude-only file in TOON (pipe-delimited; # lines are comments).
# Written 2026-10-27 from a scan of tools/concordia, tools/agents, docs/Adventure/Campaign and forge-gui/res/adventure/Concordia (import graph by script, docstrings, user answers). Read after MAIN_SESSION_BRIEF.md (START.md step 5). Update in place when files move; INDEX.md points here.
# It does not repeat rules: rules live in CLAUDE.md, MAIN_SESSION_BRIEF.md and human_logic.toon (a rule beats a metric). Paths are repo-relative. Skip tools/concordia/backups, */archive*, ai_lab/results and digests.

pipeline[8|]{stage|what happens|entry script|reads|writes}:
1 card data|Scryfall bulk + Forge card scripts are the only sources|scryfall_bulk.py|Scryfall API, forge-gui/res/cardsfolder|deckgen/scryfall/cards.json
2 tag run|card script -> ability parse -> card-level role tags (ability_tags.py) + ability-level group tags (tag_extra.py) -> variant post-pass (tag_variant.py) -> verify (tag_verify.py) -> twins (tag_twins.py); tag_run.py drives, tag_reports.py writes reports|tag_run.py run / card "Name"|card scripts, tag_extra DOC|tags/CARD_TAGS.toon (whole pool), TAG_REFERENCE.md, TAG_LEGEND.md, ABILITY_TWINS.json, NEW_TAGS_FOR_APPROVAL.md, REDUNDANCY_CHECK.md
3 pool|every Commander-legal AI-playable card with identity, tags, roles, power, popularity|pool.py (about 25 s)|tag_run, text_tags, power_scorer, EDHREC/staples inputs|deckgen/pool.pkl (not in git), pool_meta.json
4 power|deck and card power from fitted weights|power_scorer.py (weights from power_fit/fit.py)|pool.pkl, tier_rules.py, archetype_rules.py, power_fit/weights.json|score/PASS/FAIL per deck
5 build|tier decks 1..5|build.py (decks.json -> decks/tier1..3), gen_mono.py (mono decks), t1_plan.py (tier 1 fresh plan), variants.py|pool.pkl, policy_tags, themes, synergy, strategy_fit, consistency|forge-gui/res/adventure/Concordia/decks/*, staging_t1_fresh/
6 starters|commander-first player starters (5 colours, Normal + variants)|starter_build.py (steps: commander pick, build, glance review-export/review-apply, regen), starter_tune.py|pool.pkl, commander_support.py, COMMANDER_SUPPORT.toon|Concordia/staging_starters/*.dck + .picks.json (not live)
7 glance|can a reader that sees only tags match one that sees Oracle text|tagcheck/glance.py|fresh records of starter-deck cards, mtg2llm render, two reader subagents (only on the user's ask)|tagcheck/runs, tags/MTG2LLM_GAPS.toon
8 balance|PC vs NPC win rates at equal life|suite/sim_suite.py (standard), balance_lab/run_batch.py|sim/*.java via sim/run.sh, decks|balance_lab/records*.csv (BIG), REPORT.md

module_groups[14|]{path|function|connects to|notes}:
tools/concordia/deckgen/tag_run.py|tagging driver; imported by 14 modules (hub)|ability_tags, tag_extra, derived_tags, tag_twins, tag_variant, tag_verify|changes here re-key every downstream file; regenerate pool.pkl and tag outputs after any tag change
tools/concordia/deckgen/tag_extra.py|ability-level tags (human_logic H56); DOC dict is the meaning table|tag_run, tag_reports, tag_variant, reverse_check|a new family is PROPOSED until approved; add a DOC row with the code; approval constants in tag_reports.py (APPROVED, APPROVED_LATER, APPROVED_DECISION)
tools/concordia/deckgen/tag_reports.py|reports + approval doc generator (NEW_TAGS_FOR_APPROVAL.md, TAG_REFERENCE.md)|tag_run, tag_extra, tag_twins, tag_verify|generated outputs: regenerate, never hand-merge
tools/concordia/deckgen/tagcheck/mtg2llm.py|tags -> text renderer (mined rules, compose(), HAND_UNIT from hand_units.json)|tag_run, tag_hash, run_memory, common|pattern() keys are sorted tag families with numbers as N; a new tag re-keys mined rules and hand lines; hand_units.json keys are global, never key a line on a generic fragment; gaps in tags/MTG2LLM_GAPS.toon (apply open rows first)
tools/concordia/deckgen/tagcheck/reverse_check.py + glance.py + score.py|blind reader export/compare and the glance test|cards, mtg2llm, tag_extra, run_log, reader_metric|readers are subagents: only on the user's ask, check the rate limit first
tools/concordia/deckgen/tagcheck/guards.py|rule guard, gap file, tag audit (the tag guard was removed 2026-10-28: pool tags are the one record)|cards|
tools/concordia/deckgen/pool.py|builds pool.pkl|tag_run, text_tags, power_scorer (circular use with power_scorer reads pool.pkl)|pool.py --check / --if-stale / --cat
tools/concordia/power_scorer.py|deck rating vs encounter tiers; edh model from power_fit/weights.json|archetype_rules, tier_rules, pool, tag_version; used by 10 modules|rule H-numbers in human_logic override its metric
tools/concordia/tier_rules.py + archetype_rules.py|the one source of truth for tier and archetype rules|used by build, power_scorer, build_queue, starter_build|do not duplicate numbers elsewhere
tools/concordia/deckgen/build.py|tier deck builder|13 modules (ability_tags, archetype_rules, commander_support, consistency, power_scorer, strategy_fit, synergy, themes, ...)|do not run dry builds without the user's approval
tools/concordia/deckgen/starter_build.py|starter builder with land picker (coverage > utility > no tapped > no life > no sacrifice-other)|build, commander_support, consistency, gen_mono, synergy, arcmind_score|H96-H103; 729 lines, read by Grep/offset
tools/concordia/deckgen/commander_support.py + COMMANDER_SUPPORT.toon|what supports a commander's ability|ability_tags, tag_run, tag_status, tag_map|consumed by build, starter_build, themes, t1_plan
tools/concordia/strategies/*|45 archetypes, baseline roles, strategies.json|strategy_fit.py used by build, starter_build, synergy|raw/ holds fetched strategy texts (BIG)
tools/concordia/{sim,suite,balance_lab,gamerunner,ai_lab}|sims (Java, headless Forge), batch runner, AI A/B research|sim_suite and run_logs import balance_lab/build_queue + run_batch|ai_lab patches are research only; never edit forge-ai

